From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: explorer: File Explorer

The folder window laid out as Windows 10/11's File Explorer, around shell32's
ExplorerBrowser (programs/explorer/fileexplorer.c; explorer.c keeps only the
command line): a command bar (New folder/Text Document, Cut, Copy, Paste,
Rename, Delete, Properties, Sort, View with Show > Navigation pane / File name
extensions / Hidden items, and "..."); back/forward (its own history),
up, a breadcrumb address bar (This PC > Documents > ... for the user's
folders; a crumb's chevron lists its subfolders; a click on the empty part,
Ctrl+L, Alt+D or F4 edits it; typed paths, ::{CLSID}, %VARS%, Unix paths and
programs work), refresh, a search box (Ctrl+F/F3/Ctrl+E) that searches the
folder and below on a thread and shows the results in place (Name, Folder,
Date modified, Type, Size; open, open file location, context menu); a
navigation pane (Quick access, This PC with its folders and drives,
Network), drawn by us; a status bar (items, selection and its size, the
details/large icons switch). This PC is its own page: Folders, and Devices
and drives with capacity bars. With no arguments explorer opens This PC.
`explorer /select,FILE` selects the file (also in a window already open
there). Keys: Ctrl+Shift+N, F2, Del (to the Recycle Bin, no question, as
Windows 10), Shift+Del, Alt+Enter, Ctrl+A/C/X/V, Alt+Left/Right/Up,
Backspace, F5, Ctrl+N, Ctrl+W, F6/Tab. Per-folder view mode, window size and
navigation pane width are remembered in HKCU\Software\Stained Glass\Explorer.
Icons are our own line glyphs drawn with GDI+.

Gate: test/explorer-gate.sh (make test-explorer).
